{"title":"Palindromic Substrings","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Given a string `s` of lowercase English letters, count how many of its substrings are palindromes.\n\nA **substring** is a contiguous block of characters. Substrings are counted by their **position** (start and end index), so equal substrings that occur at different places are counted separately. A **palindrome** reads the same forwards and backwards; every single character is a palindrome.\n\nFor example, `s = \"level\"` has the 7 palindromic substrings `l`, `e`, `v`, `e`, `l`, `eve` and `level`.\n\n**Follow-up:** the interviewer started from a 2D table `dp[i][j]` meaning 'is `s[i..j]` a palindrome' and then asked how to avoid the `O(n^2)` memory by expanding around centres. A linear-time algorithm (Manacher) also exists.","inputFormat":"A single line containing the string `s`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the number of palindromic substrings.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s| ≤ 2000","`s` consists of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"level","output":"7","explanation":"The five single letters, plus `eve` and `level`, give 7."},{"input":"abab","output":"6","explanation":"The four single letters, plus `aba` (positions 0-2) and `bab` (positions 1-3), give 6."},{"input":"aaa","output":"6","explanation":"Three single letters, two substrings `aa` (positions 0-1 and 1-2) and one `aaa` give 6."}],"tests":[{"input":"a","output":"1"},{"input":"ab","output":"2"},{"input":"aa","output":"3"},{"input":"aba","output":"4"},{"input":"abba","output":"6"},{"input":"abc","output":"3"},{"input":"aaaa","output":"10"},{"input":"abcba","output":"7"},{"input":"zyxxyz","output":"9"},{"input":"bab","output":"4"},{"input":"kqg","output":"3"},{"input":"aaaaaa","output":"21"},{"input":"aaaaab","output":"16"},{"input":"bbbacb","output":"9"},{"input":"wxckzz","output":"7"},{"input":"aaaaaaaaaa","output":"55"},{"input":"aaabaaabaa","output":"25"},{"input":"ccbcccbcac","output":"20"},{"input":"","output":"200100